# Multi-objective optimization in competition for subsurface resources -- Bjarmeland Formation

Scripts for performing multi-objective optimization for pressure-dominated CO$_2$ storage problems with setup for Test case IV: Bjarmeland formation with nine wells, 
as described in:
> Pettersson, P., Krumscheid, S. and Gasda, S. (2025) "Cooperative games defined by multi-objective optimization in competition for subsurface resources." arXiv preprint arXiv:2502.19987. 

A model for the Bjarmeland Formation in Barents Sea is inititalized via the Matlab Reservoir Simulation Toolbox (MRST). Multi-objective optimization is then performed using either NSGA-II, or the weighted sum method.


## Requirements
* MATLAB (tested with R2025b)
* Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox in MATLAB
* PlatEMO (tested with release 4.16) https://github.com/BIMK/PlatEMO
* MRST (tested with release 2026a) https://www.sintef.no/projectweb/mrst/download/
* Set-Partition (tested with version 1.6.0) https://se.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/24133-set-partition/files/SetPartFolder

## Installation
1. Clone the repository or download the source files.
2. Download PlatEMO, MRST, and Set-Partition (available through links above) to the root folder.

## Quick Start / Usage
1. Open MATLAB and navigate to the project root folder.
2. Open the main file ```main_generate_MOO_results.m```
and choose either ```sol_meth = 'MOO'``` for use of NSGA-II,
or ```sol_meth = 'WSM'``` to use the weighted sum method.
Set the evolutionary algorithm parameters ```N_SO``` (population size, initialization), ```maxFE_init``` (max func eval for each initial point), ```N``` (population size MOO), and ```maxFE``` (max func eval for MOO), 
for an appropriate tradeoff between computational cost and accuracy.
3. Run the main script or function from the MATLAB Command Window:

```matlab
main_generate_MOO_results;
```
3. For the first time running, answer yes ('Y') to downloading reservoir data via MRST.
4. To visualize the results, run
```matlab
plot_Pareto_fronts;
```



## Notes for use
* The settings for the parameters of the evolutionary algorithms in ```matlab plot_Pareto_fronts.m``` need to match those
used in ```main_generate_MOO_results.m``` (or any other existing simulation results).

* The computational cost for running well-resolved multi-objective optimization for all coalition
structures is very high, so it might be worthwhile running independent coalition structures in parallel, or using the hierarchical property
proven in Pettersson et al (2025) to reduce computational cost.

* MRST prints out warning messages that can be ignored. The Bjarmeland setup has not been modified from the MRST source files.

* Comment out L269 (step_header(i);) in simulateScheduleAD.m in MRST to save computational time.


