# Multi-objective optimization in competition for subsurface resources: Bjarmeland Formation

Scripts for multi-objective optimization of pressure-limited CO$_2$ storage, set up for Test case IV (the Bjarmeland Formation with nine wells) in:

> Pettersson, P., Krumscheid, S. and Gasda, S. (2025) "Cooperative games defined by multi-objective optimization in competition for subsurface resources." arXiv preprint [arXiv:2502.19987](https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.19987).

A model of the Bjarmeland Formation in the Barents Sea is set up with the MATLAB Reservoir Simulation Toolbox (MRST). For every coalition structure of the three agents, the Pareto front of the coalitions' injected CO$_2$ is then computed with either NSGA-II or the weighted sum method, subject to a pressure limit of 90% of the overburden pressure.

## Requirements
* MATLAB (tested with R2025b) with the Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox
* [PlatEMO](https://github.com/BIMK/PlatEMO) (tested with release 4.16)
* [MRST](https://www.sintef.no/projectweb/mrst/download/) (tested with release 2026a)
* [Set-Partition](https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/24133-set-partition) (tested with version 1.6.0)

## Installation
1. Clone the repository or download the source files.
2. Download PlatEMO, MRST and Set-Partition into the repository root. The scripts expect these folder names:
   ```
   <repo root>/
   ├── PlatEMO/
   ├── mrst-2026a/        (any folder starting with "mrst" that contains startup.m)
   ├── Set-Partition/
   └── *.m
   ```

## Usage
1. Open MATLAB in the repository root.
2. Set the options in `problem_config.m`:
   * `sol_meth = 'MOO'` for NSGA-II, or `'WSM'` for the weighted sum method;
   * the algorithm parameters `N_SO` (population size, initialization), `maxFE_init` (max function evaluations per initial point), `N` (population size) and `maxFE` (max function evaluations), trading computational cost against accuracy;
   * `seed`, the random seed.
3. Run the optimization:
   ```matlab
   main_generate_MOO_results
   ```
   The first time, answer yes (`Y`) when MRST asks to download the CO2 Storage Atlas data.
4. Plot the results:
   ```matlab
   plot_Pareto_fronts
   ```

Results are written to `results_<sol_meth>_NW_9/`, one subfolder per coalition structure, together with the settings used (`cfg.mat`).

## Notes
* Both scripts read their settings from `problem_config.m`, so the plots always match the latest run. To plot older results, set the same parameters there.
* Optimizing all coalition structures is expensive. Coalition structures are independent, so they can be run in parallel by setting `CS_to_run` in `main_generate_MOO_results.m`, or the cost can be reduced with the hierarchical property proven in Pettersson et al. (2025).
* MRST prints warning messages that can be ignored.

